{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:UGB.UnitalGroebner.pbw_corollary","@type":"LeanModule","name":"UGB.UnitalGroebner.pbw_corollary","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Basic","lean:module:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.CompositionLemma"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.UnitalGroebner.pbw_corollary","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.UnitalGroebner.pbw_corollary","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/UnitalGroebner/pbw_corollary.lean#L53-L83","doc":"**PBW corollary — canonical-form core.**\n\nPresenting `U𝔤` by a Gröbner–Shirshov basis `sys`, every element\nreduces to a normal form (a PBW monomial / element of `S𝔤`), and any\ntwo normal forms of the same element coincide. This is the bijective\nPBW correspondence `U𝔤 ↔ S𝔤` at the canonical-form level.\n\nThe conclusion is a **concrete conjunction over `AlgElement`** — a\n`ReducesToNF` existential plus a `∀`-uniqueness clause — the\nsubstantive content the former `holds : Prop` lacked. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:cor:pbw","label":"cor:pbw","md":"unital-groebner-bases/unital-groebner-bases-chapter/pbw-corollary.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}